@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam ArrowColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #17405A
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #4A302B
skinparam noteBorderColor #F1AD8A
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox
autonumber
title MVP + EXPLICIT FUTURE PATHS — SB-M09 — Independent refinement, Sprint planning and Sprint-end actions
actor "Authorized participant" as U
participant "Work project" as P
participant "Backlog Item / Task" as I
participant "[AFTER MVP] Sprint / Sprint Backlog" as S
U -> P : Request one intended work operation
P -> P : Check current resource authority and state
alt Denied or conflicting context
 P --> U : Denial / conflict; no completed-change claim
else Permitted current operation
 alt Refine Backlog Item
  P -> I : Retain distinct item/task relationships and assignment
  I --> U : Actual refinement outcome
 else Maintain Sprint Backlog
  P -> S : Review goal, selected items and delivery plan
  S -> I : Validate permitted intended selections
  I --> S : Eligible / invalid / conflicting context
  S --> U : Actual coherent-plan result or rejection
 else Separately end / cancel Sprint
  P -> S : Evaluate permitted end and actual outcome
  S -> I : Identify accepted / incomplete work
  I --> S : Actual item status / history context
  S --> U : Recorded goal/outcome and explicit incomplete-work disposition
 end
end
note over I,S
Independent goals, not one mandatory sequence.
Task/card state alone is not item acceptance or Sprint success.
end note
legend bottom
Logical domain interaction, not runtime execution evidence.
Detailed proposed guards/policies retain their primary status.
endlegend
@enduml
